1a56e6b2-bb9e-4c34-af15-b493ab3b8b07	022b192e-890a-44bb-94a7-bbd68b848a58	assistant	The standard **Customer Order Procedure** in Vector ERP follows these key stages:\n\n1. **Lead & Client Management (CRM):**\n   - **Leads & Clients (`clients`):** New prospects are registered in the system as leads or clients. Contact details and interactions are managed through the CRM module (`client_contacts`, `site_visits`).\n\n2. **Order Placement (`orders` & `order_items`):**\n   - Once a client confirms their requirements, a sales order is created containing the requested items, quantities, and pricing.\n\n3. **Invoicing & Payments (`invoices`, `invoice_items`, & `payments`):**\n   - Proforma or sales invoices are generated from the order. \n   - Payments received from the client are recorded against the invoices.\n\n4. **Design Process (`designs`, `design_versions`, & `design_communications`):**\n   - If the order requires custom artwork or layouts, design tasks are attached to the order.\n   - Designers upload revisions, and front-desk staff communicate feedback back and forth with the client.\n\n5. **Production & Job Orders (`production_orders`, `job_orders`):**\n   - Once the design is approved and payment/invoicing milestones are met, the order moves to production.\n   - Job orders and manufacturing orders are generated to track the production process across machines (`machines`, `machine_maintenance_logs`).\n\n6. **Delivery & Installation (`deliveries` & `installations`):**\n   - Finished goods are dispatched via delivery records, and installation services are scheduled and completed at the client's site if applicable.	2026-09-25 13:09:43.412612+00
